-07,-2.264974000354414e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10048,2900,279,19703,315,279,47311,400,87,61,17,481,14619,488,308,3,525,6785,10250,25780,320,1921,14312,12460,568,16246,429,400,76,366,220,17,15,4779,1246,1657,3204,2750,315,400,77,3,525,1052,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSuppose the roots of the polynomial $x^2 - mx + n$ are positive prime integers (not necessarily distinct). Given that $m < 20,$ how many possible values of $n$ are there?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5cf7b8ca305c7d7a025959f056cbc91266a163b7c576ce4ace732a5d90287f98"},"seconds":86.49336242675781,"seed":880980113098377633,"stop":"eos","text":"Given the polynomial \\(x^2 - mx + n\\) with roots that are positive prime integers, let's denote the roots by \\(p\\) and \\(q\\). According to Vieta's formulas, we have:\n\\[ m = p + q \\]\n\\[ n = pq \\]\n\nSince \\(m < 20\\), we need to consider all pairs of positive prime numbers \\(p\\) and \\(q\\) such that their sum is less than 20. We will list all such pairs and calculate the corresponding values of \\(n = pq\\).\n\nThe prime numbers less than 20 are: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19. We will consider all pairs \\((p, q)\\) where \\(p \\leq q\\) to avoid duplicate pairs.\n\n1. If \\(p = 2\\):\n   - \\(q = 2\\): \\(m = 2 + 2 = 4\\), \\(n = 2 \\cdot 2 = 4\\)\n   - \\(q = 3\\): \\(m = 2 + 3 = 5\\), \\(n = 2 \\cdot 3 = 6\\)\n   - \\(q = 5\\): \\(m = 2 + 5 = 7\\), \\(n = 2 \\cdot 5 = 10\\)\n   - \\(q = 7\\): \\(m = 2 + 7 = 9\\), \\(n = 2 \\cdot 7 = 14\\)\n   - \\(q = 11\\): \\(m = 2 + 11 = 13\\), \\(n = 2 \\cdot 11 = 22\\)\n   - \\(q = 13\\): \\(m = 2 + 13 = 15\\), \\(n = 2 \\cdot 13 = 26\\)\n   - \\(q = 17\\): \\(m = 2 + 17 = 19\\), \\(n = 2 \\cdot 17 = 34\\)\n   - \\(q = 19\\): \\(m = 2 + 19 = 21\\) (not valid since \\(m < 20\\))\n\n2. If \\(p = 3\\):\n   - \\(q = 3\\): \\(m = 3 + 3 = 6\\), \\(n = 3 \\cdot 3 = 9\\)\n   - \\(q = 5\\): \\(m = 3 + 5 = 8\\), \\(n = 3 \\cdot 5 = 15\\)\n   - \\(q = 7\\): \\(m = 3 + 7 = 10\\), \\(n = 3 \\cdot 7 = 21\\)\n   - \\(q = 11\\): \\(m = 3 + 11 = 14\\), \\(n = 3 \\cdot 11 = 33\\)\n   - \\(q = 13\\): \\(m = 3 + 13 = 16\\), \\(n = 3 \\cdot 13 = 39\\)\n   - \\(q = 17\\): \\(m = 3 + 17 = 20\\) (not valid since \\(m < 20\\))\n\n3. If \\(p = 5\\):\n   - \\(q = 5\\): \\(m = 5 + 5 = 10\\), \\(n = 5 \\cdot 5 = 25\\)\n   - \\(q = 7\\): \\(m = 5 + 7 = 12\\), \\(n = 5 \\cdot 7 = 35\\)\n   - \\(q = 11\\): \\(m = 5 + 11 = 16\\), \\(n = 5 \\cdot 11 = 55\\)\n   - \\(q = 13\\): \\(m = 5 + 13 = 18\\), \\(n = 5 \\cdot 13 = 65\\)\n   - \\(q = 17\\): \\(m = 5 + 17 = 22\\) (not valid since \\(m < 20\\))\n\n4. If \\(p = 7\\):\n   - \\(q = 7\\): \\(m = 7 + 7 = 14\\), \\(n = 7 \\cdot 7 = 49\\)\n   - \\(q = 11\\): \\(m = 7 + 11 = 18\\), \\(n = 7 \\cdot 11 = 77\\)\n   - \\(q = 13\\): \\(m = 7 + 13 = 20\\) (not valid since \\(m < 20\\))\n\n5. If \\(p = 11\\):\n   - \\(q = 11\\): \\(m = 11 + 11 = 22\\) (not valid since \\(m < 20\\))\n\n6. If \\(p = 13\\):\n   - \\(q = 13\\): \\(m = 13 + 13 = 26\\) (not valid since \\(m < 20\\))\n\n7. If \\(p = 17\\):\n   - \\(q = 17\\): \\(m = 17 + 17 = 34\\) (not valid since \\(m < 20\\))\n\n8. If \\(p = 19\\):\n   - \\(q = 19\\): \\(m = 19 + 19 = 38\\) (not valid since \\(m < 20\\))\n\nThe possible values of \\(n\\) are: 4, 6, 9, 10, 14, 15, 21, 22, 25, 26, 33, 34, 35, 39, 49, 55, 65, 77. There are 18 distinct values.\n\nTherefore, the number of possible values of \\(n\\) is \\(\\boxed{18}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{18}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
